From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: owner <owner@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:02:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] Taviri desktop: own name, icon, ids and data, next to
 Bitwarden

The Bitwarden desktop app built as "Taviri", installable next to the
official app without sharing anything with it.

- Name read from the extension's smartfill-brand/brand.json (one setting
  for both); ids in apps/desktop/taviri/brand.json: bundle id
  io.github.perlytiara.taviri.desktop, data folder "Taviri Desktop",
  taviri:// scheme, native messaging host io.github.perlytiara.taviri,
  SSH agent socket ~/.taviri-ssh-agent.sock.
- Native messaging manifests under Taviri's own name, allowing only the
  Taviri extension; Bitwarden's com.8bit.bitwarden files are never
  written or removed. No DuckDuckGo manifest.
- IPC socket folder and SSH socket name set at compile time
  (TAVIRI_APP_ID, TAVIRI_SSH_SOCK_NAME); no App Group in Info.plist.
- Auto-update off; SSO always through the localhost callback.
- About panel, description and NOTICE.txt say it is based on Bitwarden
  (GPL-3.0); LICENSE_GPL.txt ships in the app.
- Icons drawn from the brand kit (taviri/make-icons.js); app-name strings
  renamed in all locales; window title from the brand.
- Unsigned arm64 packaging: taviri/electron-builder.taviri.js and
  after-pack.taviri.js (same fuses as upstream releases).

Details: apps/desktop/taviri/CHANGES.md

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
